---
description: Common rules for React components across all projects
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
- All React components must use TypeScript with proper type definitions
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all component props
- Keep components simple and focused on a single responsibility
- Keep components dumb and reusable
- Always use Tailwind CSS for styling (no custom CSS or @apply directives)
- Use Tailwind CSS exclusively for styling (no inline styles or CSS modules)
- Follow utility-first CSS approach
- Never use custom CSS or @apply directives
- Maintain consistent spacing using Tailwind's spacing scale
- Use Tailwind's color palette for consistency
- Implement responsive design using Tailwind breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)
- Use shadcn/ui components as the foundation for UI elements
- Import types from `@/lib/definitions` for shared data types
- Prefer composition over complex props
- Follow existing component patterns in the codebase
